<title>FRANCE: Marseille top French regional cargo airport in Jan.</title>
<headline>Marseille top French regional cargo airport in Jan.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's top ten regional airports for flown airfreight in January-March 1997, with percentage change on the same period last year, were as follows:</p>
<p>    1.  Marseille					 10,773   tonnes - 0.1</p>
<p>    2.  Basle-Mulhouse *				10,537   tonnes - 4.0</p>
<p>    3.  Toulouse					   6,302   tonnes - 2.0</p>
<p>    4.  Lyon-Satolas				     5,728   tonnes  +7.7</p>
<p>    5.  Lille **					   5,938   tonnes  +6.0</p>
<p>    6.  Nice						 4,123   tonnes  +3.7</p>
<p>    7.  Bordeaux					   1,809   tonnes - 9.0</p>
<p>    8.  Montpellier					1,300   tonnes  +8.0</p>
<p>    9.  Strasbourg					 1,139   tonnes -33.9</p>
<p>    10. Rennes					     1,013   tonnes +69.0</p>
<p>     *   includes traffic  handled in Swiss zone of airport</p>
<p>    **   also includes trucked air freight</p>
<p>The figures do not include France's major gateways for airfreight, Paris.CDG and Paris/Orly. -- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542-7706 Fax+5017</p>
